# Temperance — rename nuke-install → nuke-and-fresh-install

- date: 2026-09-29
- branch: chore/rename-nuke-install-to-nuke-and-fresh-install
- scope-class: b (adopter-facing script rename)

Right thing: operator asked for clearer name — script does both a nuke AND a fresh install; original name buried the install half. Rename ships now while adopter reach is zero (script merged as PR #288 minutes ago, no CDN, no npm ship).

Simplest: git mv three files (script + tests + UC doc), update internal refs, register in standards/file-renames.json per .claude/rules/file-rename-discipline.md, PR + merge.

Impact: no external adopters yet. Substrate ships the rename registry entry so any future adopter carrying the old filename gets caught by migrate-adopter-references.sh.

Verification: tests still 14/14 GREEN after rename; full suite 498/498 GREEN.

Reversibility: revert PR; rename registry keeps the trail.

Drift trigger: touching script logic OR test assertions OR UC content beyond filename swaps.
